/* THE AWAKENING - The Raccoon Attacks */
/* This is THE THING in a Ford F-150 */
/* Approximate page count: 1.5-2 pages */
/* Power arc: FALSE SECURITY -> SURVIVAL */
/* Tone: GENUINE HORROR. Not cartoon violence. */

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK (MOVING) - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS

Danny reaches for the radio dial.

DANNY
(trailing off from confession)
...almost home.

His fingers brush the knob.

CLOSE ON: The raccoon's face.

Its eyes are OPEN.

Not drowsy. Not confused. WIDE. ALERT. LOCKED on Danny's
hand as it passes six inches from its snout.

The raccoon's head TRACKS the movement. Smooth. Mechanical.
A targeting system acquiring.

Danny doesn't see. He's watching the road.

His hand returns to the wheel.

The raccoon's eyes follow.

ANGLE ON: Danny.

He glances over. Casual. Just checking on--

His face FREEZES.

For a half-second, neither moves. Man and animal. Locked
in mutual recognition.

DANNY
Oh--

The raccoon LAUNCHES.

No warning. No transition. One frame still, the next:
AIRBORNE.

CLAWS rake across Danny's face. He SCREAMS--a raw,
animal sound ripped from somewhere primal. Blood
sprays the windshield.

The truck SWERVES.

DANNY (CONT'D)
NO NO NO NO--

He grabs the raccoon. Hurls it against the passenger
window. The thing BOUNCES back, scrabbling across the
dashboard, knocking papers everywhere.

EXT. HIGHWAY - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS

WIDE ON: The truck careening across lanes. Brake lights
painting the asphalt red.

Inside the cab: SILHOUETTES THRASHING. A nightmare
shadow-puppet show.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK (MOVING) - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS

Danny holds the wheel with one hand. The other SWATS
at the raccoon as it scrambles up his chest.

DANNY
GET OFF GET OFF--

The raccoon's CLAWS find his shoulder. Dig in. Use
him as a ladder.

It's going for his FACE again.

Danny throws his head back. The raccoon's teeth SNAP
shut on empty air, inches from his nose.

The horn BLARES as his elbow hits it.

The raccoon SCREAMS.

Not a chitter. Not a hiss. A SCREAM. High-pitched.
Almost human. The sound of something that should not
exist wearing the body of something that does.

The truck jumps the center line.

HEADLIGHTS fill the windshield. HORN blaring from
oncoming--

Danny YANKS the wheel. The truck fishtails. Tires
SHRIEK against asphalt.

The raccoon loses its grip. Tumbles into the footwell.

One second. Maybe two.

Danny GASPS. Blood runs into his eyes. He can barely
see. His hand finds the door handle--

The raccoon EXPLODES from below.

It clamps onto his forearm. Teeth SINK DEEP. Danny
watches, horrified, as the thing's jaw LOCKS. It
hangs from his arm like a furry anchor.

He SLAMS his arm against the door. Once. Twice.
The raccoon holds.

The truck drifts. Danny hauls the wheel with his
free hand. Overcorrects. The vehicle bucks.

DANNY
FUCK--

He hammers the brakes.

The raccoon FLIES forward. Hits the windshield.
CRACKS the glass in a spiderweb pattern.

Drops to the dashboard.

ANGLE ON: The raccoon.

It rises. Slowly. Deliberately.

Its fur is matted with blood--Danny's blood. Its
eyes never leave his face. One ear bent wrong from
the impact.

It looks WRONG. Broken but still running. A machine
that will not stop.

Danny's chest heaves. Blood drips from his chin onto
his uniform. His left eye is swelling shut.

The raccoon takes a step toward him.

Danny's hand finds the door handle.

The raccoon COILS.

EXT. HIGHWAY - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS

The truck sits at an angle across both lanes. Engine
running. Headlights carving into darkness.

BEAT.

The driver's door BURSTS open.

Danny FALLS out. Lands hard on asphalt. Rolls.
Scrambles to his feet.

Blood streams down his face. His uniform is SHREDDED
from collar to chest. Three deep gouges run parallel
down his cheek.

He backs away from the truck. Steps unsteady. Eyes
fixed on the open door.

DANNY
(breathing hard)
Okay. Okay okay okay.

From inside the cab: SCRATCHING sounds.

Danny keeps backing up.

The scratching stops.

Silence.

Then: The raccoon's HEAD appears in the open doorway.

It looks at Danny.

Danny looks at it.

The raccoon opens its mouth and makes that sound again.
That SCREAM. The one that sounds almost human. The one
that says: I am not finished with you.

HOLD ON Danny's face. Blood. Terror. Recognition of
something he will never be able to explain.

SMASH CUT TO BLACK.

/* End scene - approximately 1.75 pages */
/* The horror makes the comedy work. */
/* This is not cartoon violence. This is BETRAYAL. */
/* Danny just opened his soul - and got his face torn off. */
